Let me collect myself and go again. The white suit man that's been following Nobodies around for ages [https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/a-place-called-nowhere has been gone for a good long while now.] I hadn't seen him for ages and I'm pretty sure he just up and fucking died somehow. That, and he never performed public miracles like that. If he did something, it was to get at me. Or the others. So what I'm confused about is why this guy is here, what's he doing it for, and if it even is White Suit at all. I'm gonna get to the bottom of this, and also hopefully stop this dunce from getting captured by jailors.

[[/span]]



[[/div]]

-----

A man in white exited a limousine in London, his glowing face leaving a growing crowd of spectators in awe as many began recording. Whether it was some stunt or true magic, it was too good to not be shared. Among these onlookers was one whose face couldn't quite be caught, and appeared similarly to most of the others in the group-- albeit his disposition was not one of awe, but of antipathy.



The white suited man strutted towards an old woman in a wheelchair struggling to cross the road. Silenced amongst the crowd, a small click was heard.



"Pardon me, miss. May I do something for you?"



"Well I s'pose so, mister. Just quickly, please," she responded. He reached and touched her knees. At first, she was taken aback, but quickly grew invigorated as she felt brand new. She stood from her wheelchair and laughed to herself, before reaching out to shake the man's hand. He took it.



"You can thank me later," he spoke before she could even say anything -- which stunned her --and then walked away back to the car before she could press on. The aforementioned blended clicking noise could be heard again. The stern man hidden in the crowd disappeared, unnoticed.

-----

