It was 2:22 in the morning when a white limousine parked out front of an apartment complex. A man with a blinding white aura around his head and a suit of a similar color exited and began to pace down the sidewalk. He walked and walked, before suddenly stopping to listen-- he had a suspicion someone was following him. He certainly painted a big target on himself. But the only sound he heard was that of dogs barking, cars in the deep distance, and the wind gusting by his ears. He continued his pace.



He reached a gas station, and walked in to grab a drink. He stepped towards the back and as he did, could swear he caught the silhouette of a man in the window, in the corner of his eye. But when he looked, nobody was there. He must be tired.



He opened the cooler and grabbed a bottle of coke. Before he could turn around, he heard shouting from the cash register area. He faced around to see a robbery in progress. He approached the thief and tapped him on the shoulder. When he turned around, he immediately yelped at his face and fired a shot into wherever he assumed the head would be. The man in white was completely unaffected, and he slapped the gun out of the man's hand.



"Who the fuck are you?!" the thief shouted afterwards, trembling.



"Please don't be scared. Let me help you. You're a petty thief, poor yourself, trying to make ends meet. Do you have family?"



The thief frantically nodded.



"You're trying to care for them, and I know what that's like. Let me help." The man in white picked the gun from the floor and put it in his coat. "Where'd you park?"



They left the gas station, but not before the man in white left a $5 bill lying on the counter for his coke-- he knew that the money was worth more than the drink, but going an extra mile is always a good idea.



The man in the white suit sat on the hood of the thief's van and had a talk with him about the importance of life and options to resort to that don't amount to crime. The thief left the conversation feeling uplifted and ready to face the darkness with his family. Before he drove away, the man in white handed his gun back to him.



"This is yours. Use this for good purposes."



As the van left, the man in the white suit locked eyes with a shadow figure standing across the lot. When he blinked, he only caught its coat disappearing behind a corner. He raised an eyebrow before hurrying back to the limo.

