[[module Rate]]

[[/>]]



I’ll find you

In halls of death that feel so cold

In Midas’s pillars made of gold

In ruins that date beyond ancient old

I’ll find you



In our locked up cells

We dream of riding out at dawn

The world moves and shifts

Just outside of these iron bars

And something in me sifts



I’ll find you

Somewhere above the windy skies

Somewhere below those nasty lies

Somewhere to see your emerald eyes

I’ll find you



They’ll keep us here

In their petting zoo

While we wait for the world to change

I hope that you’ll be by my side

During our great escapade



I’ll find you

Beyond the grand old milky way

Beyond the deepest, largest bay

Beyond the restrictions, beyond what they say



I’ll find you a place in our great escapade



