++++ Site Overview & History

[[/span]]

----

[[div style="text-align:left"]]

##transparent|......##Site-163 is the last of its kind. Before the standardization of the Foundation Facilities across the world, a younger Foundation required something more radical. In days before, the Foundation was stripped for cash and couldn't keep more than a couple of fully-furnished facilities, a serious problem when considering anomalies can turn up anywhere and anytime. In response, the Foundation employed a doctrine of quick assembly and disassembly. With time, however, [https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/pickman-blank-proposal as funds grew], the Foundation shifted toward a doctrine of permanent holdouts to better meet the growing needs of the world.



##transparent|......##Although Site-163 is spread across dozens of Foundation facilities today, Site-163 was originally a rapid anomalous humanoid detainment and containment facility operating in and around Central Europe relying on the ability to quickly set up and demolish small facilities. Site-163 provided a wealth of information about reality-benders, most of it still dictating the basics of our understanding of reality bending and policy regarding reality-benders.



##transparent|......##At the turn of the 20th century, multiple government-backed occult organizations were formed to combat, study, and eventually weaponize anomalies. Site-163, due to its more overt presence in comparison to its sister sites, became a target of raids by said organizations and expulsions by their benefactor governments. Around 63% of Site-163 onboard facilities either fell or became nonoperational. Most agree that the withering of Site-163 was due to its lax security and that Site-163 was spread too thin. On August 1923, Site-163 was officially dissolved.



##transparent|......##Unofficially, however, Site-163 was reorganized. All research and military personnel were reassigned to more conventional facilities and Site-163 was temporarily placed under direct O5 Council command. Around this time, the Intelligence Agency had been commissioned from the defunct Intelligence Community's External Espionage Bureau. Given the Foundation had publicly decommissioned Site-163, the O5 Council decided to fold Site-163 into the Intelligence Agency as an independent facility.



##transparent|......##For the inital 23 years, Site-163 was a roaming facility. Utilizing old contractors, abandoned buildings, front companies, Site-163 was a site of constantly shifting size and location. Under this model, the Agency rapidly grew and became extremely efficient in its efforts; however, data loss was common incident and on occasion failed to prevent circumstances that were entirely in their control.



##transparent|......##This model was officially put out of use in light of the Insurgency's actions in 1948. During this defection, 30% of Site-163's facilities defected or were raided by the Chaos Insurgency and its various partners. This defection led to the emergency suspension of the Intelligence Agency, and by proxy Site-163. After a thorough investigation, the Intelligence Agency was allowed to regain its autonomy under the condition Site-163 could quickly be occupied by regular Foundation forces should the need arise, a means by the Council to keep the Agency in check.



Secret Directive #7791 was passed by the O5 Council on March 23rd, 1949, a move to reestablish the Intelligence Agency as follows:

* The Agency may not be stringent in standard Foundation administrative protocols.

* The Agency may act of its own accord against GoIs so long as it cannot be traced back to the Foundation.

* The Agency is wholly responsible for the safety of its operators and not the Foundation at large.

* The Agency may not actively work against the Foundation itself; even if it will help the Foundation in the long term.

* If deemed necessary by the O5 Council, all documentation is to be handed over to the Council without complaint.

* Site-163 will be reestablished as a forwarding base of operations for the Agency.

* Site-163 will follow the doctrine of covertly operating in other Foundation facilities.

* The O5 Council and proxies will assist in the coverup of these facilities from Foundation Personnel.



##transparent|......##Site-163 is the last of its kind and the first of another. Melded from necessity and distrust, Site-163 operates across the world hidden in plain sight. We act in places where people don't like to look, where they forget. Behind the shiny labs and opulent meeting rooms, tucked behind closets and storage rooms is where we protect our unknowing comrades.[[/div]]



**//A dead site for a dead department, created by a dead man.//**



