Things had never gotten this far before. It was more than just a little odd to be confronted not only by //eagerness//, but an equally motivated party. Mihai's lips pursed as his eyes narrowed at the 'typing' indicator, considering potentially just how desperate he was to have a sponsorship with this little venture. This was the first time he was having doubts, and there was no worse time to get cold feet.



His fingers hovered over the terminal keyboard, a number of explanations spanning his thoughts. Was he going to have to defend himself again in some moral dilemma that served only to waste valuable time and resources? One hand retracted as his eyes jammed shut, involuntarily recalling a painful moment of clarity following a rather intense online argument. As he pinched his nose, emitting a pained note of remorse, Mihai prayed to never lose his temper with these sub-humans again.



Most of them had a way of getting on his nerves. Time and time again he was forced to realign his priorities, in case he indulged in the more laborious task of venting his frustrations on online pundits.



So long as the money kept flowing from his Appalachian sources, he could, at least, afford to dignify his doubters with a vitriolic reply. Mihai forced his attentions back on the screen, noting the user had finally deigned to reply.



