Mihai had never really considered the possibility that someone would be so onboard as to engineer a total team up. It was starting to look like one of those Yankee comics, hopefully lacking any of the same //corn//. Still, all things considered, that went pretty smooth. Whoever this guy was, they either lacked outward empathy for human suffering, or they were so blinded by the end goal, that they couldn't predict what was going to occur along this little endeavor. Just like the comics, there was always a good friend to die to further the heroes journey.



There was that little issue with the //geas//, but Mihai wasn't too terribly worried. There was always ways to get around them without compromising his position within it. He leaned back in his steel chair, balancing on the back legs as he rubbed at his eyes. The mage emitted a soft groan, only now becoming cognizant of the time. With the //Nazarene// safely in the hands of a fellow collaborator, it wasn't long until their work could be started.



His eyes travelled to a rather dingy looking cot on the far end of his room. It would probably take the bastard another hour just to sift through the surface level annotations, much less the entire 'summary'--which was a stupid name anyways. How could a 'summary' be 24 fucking pages long. What sense did that make?



The legs squeaked on the wooden floor as Mihai rose to his feet. A shower would fill the gap between now, and the next phase of their planning. Pulling his shirt off, he stared back down at the computer screen. //GrandOrderT// wasn't typing, so that gave Mihai all the time in the world to grab a little snack on the way. He turned smartly on his heel, uneven steps guiding him across the room, and out into the hall.



There soon after, the screen lit up again. Of course, after Mihai had grown tired of waiting.

